   stage: Origin is the runway centreline at the lift-off point. Positive x runs horizontally along the runway toward its far end; positive y is right when facing positive x; z is height above runway pavement. Aircraft coordinates refer to its fuselage centre, with its lowest extended tires 2.35 metres below that reference. Both cameras remain at negative y. The aircraft travels straight at 80 metres per second horizontally with a steady 10-degree climb angle.; x toward runway
   tone: Calm, precise and quietly consequential.
   ambience: Continuous single-engine jet roar with light airfield wind; no voices or other aircraft.
